01:13:23.480 --> 01:13:36.369
Cole Medin: And because Archon workflows, the different coding agents communicate through handoffs, we don't actually lose any progress, because, like, if we have to restart the implement, well, we'll just go back off of the plan here, right? So we don't have to, like, restart the entire Archon workflow.

430
01:13:37.760 --> 01:13:54.789
Cole Medin: And then, if you're talking about, like, failures, as in it just, like, doesn't do a good job in a certain node, I mean, that's where you can add human in the loop. So that actually is yet another really good thing about Archon, is human in the loop. So we can make it so that, like, after implementation, the Archon workflow will literally pause itself.

431
01:13:54.980 --> 01:14:08.760
Cole Medin: And then you can, like, you can work with Archon in the CLI, we have a web UI, you can talk to it in an adapter, like Slack or Discord, like, there'll be a notification for you there to then review the implementation, and you can approve it or reject it.

432
01:14:09.010 --> 01:14:29.320
